---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { TOOLS } from '../tools/registry';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="Nhako Tools is a set of file and developer utilities that run entirely in your browser. No upload, no account, no ads."
  path="/about"
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-2xl px-4 py-12 sm:px-6">
    <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight">About</h1>

    <div class="mt-7 space-y-6 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted">
      <p class="text-base text-text">
        {TOOLS.length} utilities for PDFs, media, images and code — all of which run on your
        device rather than on a server.
      </p>

      <p>
        Most online tools work by uploading your file, processing it somewhere else, and
        sending it back. That means an upload wait, a queue, a size cap, usually a daily
        limit, and often an account before you can download the result. None of that is
        necessary any more: browsers can do this work directly.
      </p>

      <p>
        So these tools have no upload step. That makes them faster — usually finished
        before the upload would have completed — and it happens to make them private,
        because a file that is never sent anywhere cannot leak. See
        <a class="text-accent underline underline-offset-2" href="/privacy">Privacy</a>
        for how to verify that claim rather than trust it.
      </p>

      <p>
        No ads, no trackers, no cookie banner, no upsell. The site is open source under
        the MIT licence — the
        <a class="text-accent underline underline-offset-2" href="https://github.com/kimzam30/Nhako-tools" rel="noopener noreferrer">source is on GitHub</a>
        if you want to read it or run it yourself.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
